      "kind": "plain",
      "text": "校庭をはさんで校舎が二{}建っています。それぞれに教室が十室あります。",
      "en": "Two school buildings stand on opposite sides of the schoolyard. Each contains ten classrooms.",
      "noun": "校庭の両側の校舎",
      "phrase": "二棟",
      "reading": "にとう",
      "readingAnswers": [
        "にとう",
        "ふたむね"
      ],
      "good": [
        "棟",
        "二棟",
        "軒",
        "二軒",
        "つ",
        "二つ",
        "個",
        "二個"
      ],
      "kana": [
        "にとう",
        "ふたむね",
        "とう",
        "むね",
        "けん",
        "にけん",
        "ふたつ",
        "こ",
        "にこ"
      ],
      "distractors": [
        "錠",
        "通",
        "匹"
      ],
      "note": "棟 counts the two whole buildings, not their classrooms. 軒 and generic object counts are also accepted. にとう is the model; ふたむね is a documented native-pattern alternative, not a separate rule that small buildings must use it."
    },
